    {
      "id": "HfX0wOjlJV8nWHdI2iIZW",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 886.51953125,
      "y": 797.2578125,
      "width": 752.5194702148438,
      "height": 25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#e03131",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b6p",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1613366769,
      "version": 131,
      "versionNonce": 739331295,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1786318020144,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1) How can we ensure strong consistency for bids? -- Dealing with contention",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1) How can we ensure strong consistency for bids? -- Dealing with contention",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "XKANLCksGZor9LJXc_qTd",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 887,
      "y": 837.5,
      "width": 619.8595581054688,
      "height": 50,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b6q",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1124643551,
      "version": 137,
      "versionNonce": 1377678481,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1786318020144,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "When multiple users bid on same auction simultaneously, we face\nrace conditions and need to ensure only 1 bid wins.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "When multiple users bid on same auction simultaneously, we face\nrace conditions and need to ensure only 1 bid wins.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "7mj4iP_Bra-k5uXNSxRqU",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 884,
      "y": 899.6171875,
      "width": 737.5994262695312,
      "height": 450,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b6r",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 497929553,
      "version": 723,
      "versionNonce": 791828735,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1786318020144,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Solution: Cache max bid in database. Our flow would look like:\n1) Lock auction row for given auction (just 1 row)\n2) Read the max bid for given auction from Auction table\n3) write the bid to DB with status of accept/reject\n4) update max bid in auction table if new bid is higher\n5) commit transaction\n\nWe could avoid pessimistic locking with OCC (optimistic concurrency control)\n1) Read auction row and get current max bid\n2) validate new bid is higher than max bid\n3) try to update auction row, only if max bid hasn't changed\n\nUPDATE auctions \nSET max_bid = :new_bid \nWHERE id = :auction_id AND max_bid = :original_max_bid\n\n4) If update succeeds, write bid record, if fail, retry from step1\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Solution: Cache max bid in database. Our flow would look like:\n1) Lock auction row for given auction (just 1 row)\n2) Read the max bid for given auction from Auction table\n3) write the bid to DB with status of accept/reject\n4) update max bid in auction table if new bid is higher\n5) commit transaction\n\nWe could avoid pessimistic locking with OCC (optimistic concurrency control)\n1) Read auction row and get current max bid\n2) validate new bid is higher than max bid\n3) try to update auction row, only if max bid hasn't changed\n\nUPDATE auctions \nSET max_bid = :new_bid \nWHERE id = :auction_id AND max_bid = :original_max_bid\n\n4) If update succeeds, write bid record, if fail, retry from step1\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
