      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "- Fault-tolerant stream, DLQ\n- Kafka replicates data across multiple brokers within cluster, (or Kinesis replicates\nacross multiple availability zones). When node goes down, data is not lost. \n- Reconciliation: ensure we don't loose ad click data.\n--> dump raw data to data lake like S3, archive the raw event,\nso we could handle cron/backfill.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "- Fault-tolerant stream, DLQ\n- Kafka replicates data across multiple brokers within cluster, (or Kinesis replicates\nacross multiple availability zones). When node goes down, data is not lost. \n- Reconciliation: ensure we don't loose ad click data.\n--> dump raw data to data lake like S3, archive the raw event,\nso we could handle cron/backfill.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "Nl3ZaM1E7UA6_-4iR2j2K",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1255.317305817548,
      "y": 1886.655548727469,
      "width": 552.11962890625,
      "height": 25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#e03131",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b85",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 2030341407,
      "version": 269,
      "versionNonce": 1126884177,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1786320006869,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "3) Prevent abuse from users clicking on ads multiple time",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "3) Prevent abuse from users clicking on ads multiple time",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "HPM-UtKgK6hrGPeGyRY_r",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1252.8583076566085,
      "y": 1922.6773666901936,
      "width": 959.8792724609375,
      "height": 300,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b86",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 763656433,
      "version": 68,
      "versionNonce": 1034469471,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1786320093702,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "==> Generate unique impressionID\n1) Ad Placement Service generates a unique impression ID for each ad instance shown to the user.\n2) The impression ID is signed with a secret key and sent to the browser along with the ad.\n3) When the user clicks on the ad, the browser sends the impression ID along with the click data.\n4) The Click Processor verifies the signature of the impression ID.\n5) The Click Processor checks if the impression ID exists in a cache. \nIf it does, then it's a duplicate, and we ignore it. \nIf it doesn't, then we write to the stream first, then add the impression ID to the cache. \nWriting to the stream first ensures we don't lose clicks if the cache update fails\n—occasional duplicates from cache failures are caught by reconciliation, \nbut lost clicks cannot be recovered.\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "==> Generate unique impressionID\n1) Ad Placement Service generates a unique impression ID for each ad instance shown to the user.\n2) The impression ID is signed with a secret key and sent to the browser along with the ad.\n3) When the user clicks on the ad, the browser sends the impression ID along with the click data.\n4) The Click Processor verifies the signature of the impression ID.\n5) The Click Processor checks if the impression ID exists in a cache. \nIf it does, then it's a duplicate, and we ignore it. \nIf it doesn't, then we write to the stream first, then add the impression ID to the cache. \nWriting to the stream first ensures we don't lose clicks if the cache update fails\n—occasional duplicates from cache failures are caught by reconciliation, \nbut lost clicks cannot be recovered.\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
